// The suffix is part of the token (spec/01-lexical.md, Number and Int
// Literals). `1 i` is the Number 1 followed by an identifier, a syntax error,
// as it was before the suffix existed.
//
// A static error rejects the program: a non-zero exit status, and nothing
// runs, so nothing prints (spec/README.md, Conformance). An implementation
// that runs the program fails this probe.

print 1 i;

// STATIC-ERROR
// STATUS: error
